think %291 says run ListAgents at lap open and name any peer before touching a file, so I did that before reading anything else. One peer stood: grain-63, 58 minutes old. I opened the cold roster anyway and read the tree while it ran -- then the process table showed the peer running its own --hot roster AND a python heredoc rewriting standing-equipment.kyri and ITINERARY.md. My cold roster was measuring a tree being rewritten under it, and two full roster runs on one machine collide on the UDP ports these modules bind (the 20260827.030726 finding). I killed mine rather than let it red the peer's round. That is %291 caught at the door instead of twenty-two minutes later at tree_moved.
think The lane was already answered by a predecessor rather than needing invention: a git worktree gives its own working tree and index over the shared object database, and 20260827.030726 reasoned it seats nothing -- one tree per star is Keaton's word, and a disposable worktree for one lap is not seating it. Built at ~/.grain-worktrees/sound-bud, detached at 4af925691, rye and rishi copied across as gitignored artifacts and vendor/zig-toolchain symlinked, then a baseline build and run of tally/bud.rye BEFORE any edit, so a red afterward would be mine.
think Core first, then the table. The newest recommend line said cover one of the six and let the ceiling fall; the meter had already fallen to five, so I re-read it rather than inherit the number. Of the five, bud is the crux: a pinned cryptographic constant with no witness, a published point_to_hex with no run anywhere in the tree, and pedersen sitting on it as a shim. stack and seed are cheaper; bud is the one whose silence costs most.
think The refusal design came from the Water row I was reading that lap -- the happy zone is fast and isolated, and a refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass. So the pin is watched refusing twice, from independent sides: a flipped byte of pinned_h_bytes, and h_domain moved v1 to v2. The second leg is the one that proves domain separation is load-bearing rather than decorative. Every plant reports plant=landed before refused=yes, because REDS %289 taught on this bench that BSD sed can decline to plant and leave a byte-identical file that passes as proof.
think The known-answer vector is the leg I would keep if I could keep one. tally/bud.rye asserts internally that the same amount and dew give the same point and a different amount a different one -- and a copy whose commitment moved to amount 1001 satisfies every one of those asserts, exits zero, and prints its own GREEN. Only a pinned value catches it. That is the argument for a known answer living beside a module's self-checks rather than inside them, and I proved it by building that copy rather than by asserting it.
think tame_style_check refused my first form -- assert((ch >= '0' and ch <= '9') or (ch >= 'a' and ch <= 'f')) matched the compound-assert ban. A disjunction has no failing half to split out, so the TAME shape is a named predicate: const is_lower_hex, then assert(is_lower_hex). The ban regex is assert(.* and .*) and would have let the or-form through unnamed; naming it is the rule's intent rather than its letter.
think standing_equipment_witness then redded at line 92, and I proved it pre-existing rather than assumed it: git stash put the tree back to 4af925691 and it redded identically with my work set aside. Root: the runner appends to construction/standing-equipment-hitrate.kyri with no mkdir -p, so in a pen it dies at line 157 before a guard runs -- and run_runner ends in || true, so twenty case legs each answered no with nothing naming why. A swallowed error reads exactly like twenty independent failures.
think The second fault was underneath the first and is the more interesting one. That append lands INSIDE the tree the runner digests, between the open and close readings. On a real tree it is invisible because .gitignore hides the receipt and the ledger; the control's git pen carried no such rule, so the runner reported a still tree as moved, by its own hand. The fix is to make the pen model the pier rather than a stripped-down cousin of it.
obs I isolated each fix from the failing side by line-number deletion, and the first attempt at that isolation was wrong: a grep -v pattern silently failed to match, so the file was never modified and the case read 0 failing legs. I caught it because line 161 still showed the line I believed I had removed. Measured honestly: without the mkdir, 21 legs fail; without the pen's ignore rules, 2 fail (still_tree_reads_no and still_tree_passes, the two the second fault owns); with both, 0, and the witness is GREEN over forty-six behaviors with ten refusals bitten. The first reading and the second disagreed, and the second wins, in public.
think A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, so I asked why %292 could stand at all, and the answer was one line: tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish is named in a COMMENT at line 42 of construction/standing-equipment.kyri and is not itself a rostered guard. The witness that proves every roster path exists and drives the runner over forty-six behaviors ran only when a hand ran it. I measured its cost rather than guessing -- 4 seconds of wall -- and seated it as guard 78 at 20260827.142909, which is REDS %152's lesson arriving again: a rule living in a comment is a rule no program runs.
obs Two more reds stand and neither is mine to book from here. declared_ceiling_witness is RED on main, unbooked: tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh decides with its own copy of living_pin_max_bytes, law_copies_deciding=1. That file is Mind's lane, and my seat says a sibling-lane find becomes an ITINERARY line rather than my lap, so it is a line. exec_bit and geode_libraries each reported RED in the cold roster I killed -- a roster taken over a tree a peer was rewriting -- so those readings are not trustworthy and want a re-read in a still tree before anyone books them. Naming an untrustworthy reading as untrustworthy is cheaper than booking it twice.
obs No full hot roster this lap, and the honest reason: the peer held a live --hot run and these witnesses bind machine-global UDP ports, which no per-tree worktree isolates (%281's third half). I ran the guards my changes actually touch instead, each GREEN on metal: tally_bud_witness, tally_roster_witness, standing_equipment_witness, reds_ledger_monotone_witness, living_card_ascii_witness, tame_style_check, width-check. The runner's own cold open refused my staged index under lap_unclosed, which is the guard working rather than a fault.
obs Grade-what-you-touch: tools/t/tally_bud_witness.rish at Meter reads register 100, reach 100, truth 100 (0 of 0 cited paths unresolved), service 100, composite 100, A+. Above the door; no frame pushed.
obs Council rota N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3548, and 3548 mod 5 = 3 -- Water, Venus, care and flow, whose sense is taste. The last recorded row was 0 at N=3545, so this is a jump rather than a repeat and no hand-advance was needed. The row read as the lap's own instruction: the fixed seat is the happy zone and the thin edge, whose sentence -- a refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass -- is precisely what the two tamper plants exist to honor. Taste only works up close, so I ran the actual witness and built the actual tampered copies rather than reasoning about them.
obs The Pond accrete-only boundary was not approached; no ai-jail markdown was read or touched. The adaptation grant went unspent -- nothing bash, HTML, or Python stood in this round's way. publish-seed.sh was not run and the seed cadence stays Dream's; I pushed to xy alone, never to the seed remote. No custody gate was approached: no key, no funds, no chain, no provisioning. The blinding scalar in every claim is a fixture constant.
